    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "Did the test indeed!\n\n> In ES5, if the argument to this method is not an object (a primitive), then it will cause a TypeError. In ES6, a non-object argument will be treated as if it was a  frozen ordinary object, simply return it.\n\nInteresting fact, from MDN.\n",
    "commit_id": "cefc1f1e3531ffce2c426410a50fe2d02df621be",
    "created_at": "2015-10-06T15:35:09Z",
